Start here
This log labels every Lean test as pass, fail or not run, and says what a pass actually proves, so students can see what works and why.
1.  Every file gets two labels: a result label (what Lean did) and a claim label (what the passing theorem proves).
2.  Every label gets a one-sentence Why in plain words, plus Lean's exact error text copied from the screen.
3.  Nothing is marked PASS or FAIL until it has been run. Notes from reading a file are marked as reading-only.
Original files are never edited. Fixes go on copies named with -fixed, and both versions are kept.
