The Why line
Every label gets one Why sentence a student can follow, under 25 words, next to Lean's exact message.
1.  Say what Lean saw, in plain words.
2.  Say which rule it teaches.
3.  Copy Lean's message and line number from the screen. Do not retype it from memory.
4.  For a PASS, say what it proves using a claim label.
Format example (an illustration, not a test result): "FAIL-SYNTAX: Lean found a closing comment marker with no opening one, so it stopped reading. Comment markers must come in pairs."
