Lessons for students
Reading this batch produced eight lessons. Each stays marked "from reading" until a Lean run confirms it.
1.  A pass is not a proof of the title. ∃ m, bilateralStep n = m passes for every function. Check the statement, not the file name. What works: label the claim strength next to the result.
2.  Examples are not "for every n". runOsc 20 7 = 1 shows one number reaches 1. Collatz needs a statement over all n. What works: label examples SPOT-CHECK.
3.  Write an unproved goal as a def. EveryOrbitEventuallyPeriodic in rebilatral states the open question without asking Lean to accept it. What works: name the target honestly, prove the true pieces around it.
4.  A ; after an inner by stays inside that block (from reading, confirm in the editor). In have h : P := by omega; simp [h], the simp runs after omega has already finished, which Lean reports as "no goals".
5.  Comment markers come in pairs. A /- needs a closing -/. MathLabHodge has an extra closer on line 77 (from reading).
6.  Copying from a phone can drift the indentation. MathLabHodge and Firefly shift right line by line. Keep each tactic block aligned, and keep the original paste too.
7.  Library paths change over time. In current Mathlib, Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic is a deprecated shim (since 2026-08-27) and the real file is Mathlib.Basic.Real.Basic. This was checked against the Mathlib source on 2026-11-24. Always record the Mathlib version with a result.
8.  Compare by hash before debating versions. Three of these files were byte-for-byte identical, and two more differed only in indentation.
